# Server and account for lifecycle/capture-ios-screenshots.sh.
# Copy to secrets/ios-screenshots.agent_visible_env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# The app runs in screenshot mode during the capture, so the library on
# this server is never shown: names and artwork are replaced with
# invented ones. Any server with a reasonably full library works.
#
# Two viewer accounts; do not use an admin account.
#
# The first is for the screens before sign-in is complete, including the
# server's terms screen. Keep it unused: the capture never agrees to the
# terms with it, so it always shows that screen.
#
# The second is for the signed-in screens. Use it for a while first
# (start some films, open a few books, play some music) so Home has
# Continue Watching and Continue Reading rows. If it is left out, the
# first account is used for everything, and its first signed-in capture
# agrees to the terms.

# Full address, as you would type it into the app's server setup screen.
MM_SNAPSHOT_SERVER_URL=https://mm.example.com
MM_SNAPSHOT_USERNAME=viewer
MM_SNAPSHOT_PASSWORD=

MM_SNAPSHOT_VIEWER_USERNAME=
MM_SNAPSHOT_VIEWER_PASSWORD=
